# Optional. Leave EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL out and the app finds the backend by itself: on the laptop Expo Go
# loaded the app from, port 8000, on whatever Wi-Fi or hotspot that is (start Expo with `npm run phone`).
#
# Set it only for a backend somewhere else, e.g.:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://fatourati.example.com
#
# Either way the backend must run on all interfaces (uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000) and
# Windows Firewall must let Python accept connections on the network you are on.
